    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Godance: sheet rows to images\n\n### How it works\nEach row of a Google Sheet becomes one Godance image job. You run the workflow by hand. It reads the sheet and takes every row that has a prompt and an empty status, one at a time: it creates the job, writes the job id to the row, then checks the job after 5 seconds and waits twice as long each time, up to 60 seconds, for at most 20 checks. A finished job writes its link and its cost in cents to the row. A row that fails gets the reason in error_message, and the workflow carries on with the next row.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a **Header Auth** credential named **Godance API**: Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer ` followed by your Godance API key. Use a key with a daily cap.\n2. Give the sheet a header row with these columns: prompt, model, size, status, job_id, output_url, cost_cents, error_message.\n3. In **Get the rows** and **Update the row**, choose your Google account, the spreadsheet and the sheet.\n4. Every row is a paid job. Price one first with `POST /v1/estimates`, and multiply by your rows.\n\n### Customization\nChange the first wait, the longest wait and the number of checks in **Start checking**. To run a row again, clear its status cell.",
        "height": 600,
        "width": 560
      },
      "id": "6bbac1b2-2fb2-49a1-a5f7-3a6195f6484c",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1160,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Read the sheet\nRows with a prompt and an empty status are run, one at a time. Every other row is left alone.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 900,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "08df3994-ccd2-4237-ab21-4751779b1c67",
      "name": "Read the sheet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1160,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Create the job\nOne image job per row. A refusal, such as no credit, a spending cap reached or an unknown model, becomes the row's error.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 680,
